This product includes material derived from Code World Model
(https://github.com/buaacyw/code-world-model), Copyright the Code World Model
authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Specifically:

1. The condition format implemented in compiler/render.py -- resolution, metric
   first-surface depth, the 0.3 m / 256 m log endpoints, the 2x2 resample, and
   the 0-11 semantic ontology -- was derived by measurement from that project's
   released example conditions and their metadata.json.

2. Scene prose in world/take_content.py derives from that project's released
   prompt files. The longest verbatim run is 12 words.

3. The six comparison figures under docs/ display that project's released
   conditions and frames generated from them, alongside our own, for the purpose
   of comparison.

No source code from that project is included in this repository.

Paper: Code World Model: Coding Agent as World Brain
       Yiwen Chen, Guosheng Lin, Chi Zhang
       arXiv:2608.25927
